From 4afa6aee7f3a8cf6f9a37f80a35fc871d0cfa098 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 18:37:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tools/dvbridge: pass 8 as it was by default; the corrections
 of pass 3 and the simplified rounding as levels

accef6e made every frame of a picture whose decoding is not affine draw the
corrections in pass 3 (another shader, an RGBA32F target of 132.7 MB) and pass
8 take them, also where nothing is drawn over the picture (PQ subtitles over a
picture made whole) and on every GPU; its bytes were proven the same on
lavapipe and through D3D12 only, not on radeonsi or NVIDIA's own compiler, while
pass 8 as 9ff2bad had it ran on both in hardware.

dvbridge_source_gui_level() now asks for the level of the conversion of the
pixels drawn over: 0, the default, pass 3 and pass 8 as 9ff2bad had them, the
same statements and the same GLSL; 1, the corrections of pass 3 (PICTURE_CORR,
and PAIRS_CORR, which is accef6e's PAIRS); 2, the simplified rounding
(PICTURE_FLAG, PAIRS_SIMPLE, as c7efaca). A level is drawn only where its
programs were made (each with the one below it, both or none) and its target
can be; else the highest below it, which is exact. dvbridge_source_gui_top()
says which levels were made.

The targets of levels 1 and 2 (132.7 and 8.3 MB) are freed by
dvbridge_source_gui_release(), for the caller to call when no frame needs them
and when native output ends; they are made again when a picture is drawn at
their level.

dvbridge_render_gui_drawn() is the level the last frame packed was drawn at:
0 for a frame not packed in the source transport (the BT.2020 transport, a
profile that pass 8 does not draw, a pack that fails), where before the value
of the frame before could stay.

Checked: at level 0, pass 3, pass 8, pass 4 after it and the making of pass 8
are statement for statement those of 1095dd0 (= 9ff2bad), and its 12 programs
the same GLSL; PAIRS_CORR and PICTURE_CORR the GLSL of accef6e, PICTURE_FLAG
and PAIRS_SIMPLE that of c7efaca. With the software bridge on the integrated
Radeon through D3D12, 14 frames (a profile 5 picture under every kind of GUI
and every way of drawing over it, a FEL and an 8.1 picture): level 1, the codes
of level 0 in all 12 profile 5 frames; level 2, the 87,488 codes of before,
none apart by more than one or outside the pixels drawn over; FEL and 8.1,
never drawn above level 0. The targets: none at level 0 (PQ subtitles over a
picture made whole included), made at their level, their textures deleted when
released, made again after.
